_package\\\":\\\".\\\",\n  \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"761ecfb0e8b14df99a7f85eacbd9b87a-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"Adds a user-Restore phase after the long run and the configuration change: a current-configuration leader snapshots, consumes the snapshot through the public Restore API and the cluster is sampled again, so the repair question's second mechanism is exercised; the earlier phases are unchanged.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"The harness now waits on a leader Barrier, takes a snapshot on a current-configuration leader, calls Restore(meta, reader, 5s) with that snapshot, waits up to 15s for the nodes' applied write lists to agree and emits a 'user_restored' event with the leader, the error, the restarted node's applied writes, whether the minority write is still present and whether all nodes agree.\\\",\n   \\\"Five comparisons are added over the new event in both modes.\\\"],\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-installsnap\\\",\\\"s-dupskip\\\",\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"s-processlogs\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"The two-mode restart scenario after the long run and the configuration change, extended with the public user-restore path: a current-configuration leader snapshots and consumes the snapshot, and the applied state of all five nodes is sampled afterwards.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The Restore call follows the pattern the repository's own snapshotAndRestore helper uses: take a snapshot with Snapshot(), open it with Open(), then call Restore(meta, reader, timeout) on the leader.\\\",\n    \\\"A Barrier is issued first because takeSnapshot refuses while the FSM has not applied the latest committed configuration entry (local feedback showed 'cannot take snapshot now, wait until the configuration entry at N has been applied').\\\",\n    \\\"The snapshot the leader consumes is one it produced itself in the same run, which models a leader-side restore of a backup rather than restoring an external file.\\\",\n    \\\"Convergence is judged by the applied write lists that the harness can observe through the MockFSM.\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No external snapshot file or separate cluster is used, and the offset manipulation the repository's own test performs is not reproduced.\\\",\n    \\\"The term-changing truncation path is still not exercised.\\\",\n    \\\"No repository test was executed.\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"modes\\\":[\\\"defect_restart\\\",\\\"control_no_restore\\\"],\\\"long_run_entries\\\":200,\\\"restore_timeout_seconds\\\":5,\\\"convergence_window_seconds\\\":15}},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The helper builds the five-node cluster with in-memory transports, stores and MockFSM, bootstraps {A,B,C} from A, elects a leader, transfers leadership to A if needed, applies three commands, snapshots A, starts D and E, adds both as voters, applies a further command and emits 'fixture'. It shuts A down, cuts {A,C} from {B,D,E}, reconnects A to C only, restarts A with the mode's feature setting and emits 'restart'. It waits for a leader per partition, writes once on each leader, reads the shared index and emits 'outcome'. It reconnects the mesh, waits for one leader, applies one entry, applies 200 further entries, waits for the long run and emits 'healed'. It then ensures a current-configuration leader, adds voter F and emits 'reconfigured'. Finally it selects a leader among B, D and E, waits on a Barrier, takes a snapshot on it, opens that snapshot and calls Restore with a five-second timeout, waits up to 15 seconds for the nodes' applied write lists to agree, and emits 'user_restored' with the leader, error, the restarted node's applied writes, whether the minority write is present and whether all nodes agree. The repair phase follows as before. The test runs mode defect_restart first and control_no_restore second.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"hashicorp/raft client contract for Restore plus the installSnapshot path it triggers on followers: the leader takes the snapshot state and pushes it to every follower that must fault to it.\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"fixture\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}]+fx},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"adm_control\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"fixture\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"control_no_restore\\\"}]+fx}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   c(\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"defect_restart\\\",\\\"user_restore_error\\\",\\\"none\\\",\\\"Feature on: the public Restore call on the leader should succeed after the FSM catches up.\\\"),\n   c(\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"defect_restart\\\",\\\"a_fsm_applied_writes_after_restore\\\",\\\"majority-write\\\",\\\"Feature on: after the restore the restarted node's applied writes should be the snapshot's, not its own minority write.\\\"),\n   c(\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"defect_restart\\\",\\\"minority_write_present_on_a_after_restore\\\",False,\\\"Feature on: the minority write should be gone from the restarted node's applied state.\\\"),\n   c(\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"defect_restart\\\",\\\"fsm_applied_consistent_after_restore\\\",True,\\\"Feature on: the user restore should converge all nodes, unlike the per-node installSnapshot path.\\\"),\n   c(\\\"adm_control\\\",\\\"control_no_restore\\\",\\\"fsm_applied_consistent_after_restore\\\",True,\\\"Feature off control: the same restore should leave the cluster consistent.\\\")]\n }}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run && cp draft/work/zz_stale_test.go draft/assurance_stale_election_test.go && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"written\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"c616cad1b86d42518c7af4bc5bffef9d\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 2817.4894598299998, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": true, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"experiments\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"experiment\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Closed the repair question's user-Restore gap by exercising the public restore path in the cluster scenario. After the long run and the configuration change the harness now has a current-configuration leader wait on a Barrier (without it takeSnapshot refuses with 'cannot take snapshot now, wait until the configuration entry at N has been applied', as local feedback showed), take a snapshot, and consume it through Restore(meta, reader, 5s) using the same pattern the repository's own snapshotAndRestore test uses, then waits up to 15 s for the nodes' applied write lists to agree. Local construction feedback in both modes: the restore succeeds and every node's applied writes converge on the majority write, with the minority write gone from the restarted node — the cluster-wide convergence the per-node installSnapshot path did not reach. The experiment is filed under the repair question as a revision of its previous experiment with the new phase described in scope and prefix, five comparisons over the new event (restore error, the restarted node's applied writes, absence of the minority write, and cluster-wide consistency in both modes), and the unfiled term-changing truncation path plus the harness-produced (rather than external) snapshot recorded as explicit limits. Incomplete: that receipt and its interpretation, and the term-changing truncation path.\"}"}}
